00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:22.340
available apps. It surfaces practical questions around trust and effectiveness. Builders in the wellness

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:26.660
space should note the reported user concerns before designing new interfaces.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:33.040
Landing agent provides a reference annotated data set and agentic generation framework for landing

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:39.820
pages. It profiles targets, builds reference guided wireframes and refines pages through critique.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:45.720
The system outperforms direct prompting on faithfulness, conciseness, and layout diversity.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.380
Web developers generating marketing pages can test the three-phase pipeline on landing bench.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:58.580
Quorum offers quality optimized routing using multiple annotators. The budget-aware router assigns

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:04.540
instances to human or LLM annotators using feature-based difficulty signals and agreement rewards.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:13.060
It improved annotation quality by up to 34.4% while cutting costs 8.8% versus prior methods.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:18.620
Teams running large annotation projects should evaluate the multi-annotator routing approach.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:23.400
Okay, let's pop the hood on the vector index approach to output embeddings.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:29.560
Everyone talks about swapping the final linear layer for a vector index as if it is a drop-in speed

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:35.320
trick. In practice, the change replaces a dense matrix multiply with an approximate nearest

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:41.640
neighbor lookup, followed by a sparse scatter of logits. The core insight is that only a small candidate

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:48.140
set of tokens ever receives non-zero probability. So exact computation over the full vocabulary is

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:56.060
unnecessary for most steps. On the Gemma 3 270 million model, this yields up to 82% higher tokens per

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:03.680
second at batch size 1 on CPU, while alpaca eval scores remain unchanged. The quality preservation holds

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:09.660
because the index retrieves the true top-k tokens with high probability. The main trade-off is a

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:14.060
small risk of missing an edge-case token that would have ranked just inside the cut-off.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:20.340
The approach works best when the vocabulary is large and multilingual, or when inference runs on

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:26.220
memory bandwidth-limited hardware. When the model is already heavily quantized or when batch sizes

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:31.900
exceed roughly 8, the relative gain shrinks and a standard dense projection may remain simpler.

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:37.760
The gacha that bites most teams is forgetting to rescore the retrieved candidates with the original

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:44.000
logits before sampling. Without that step, the generation distribution drifts. So when should you

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:50.720
actually reach for this versus the alternative? It shines on small batch CPU runs with large vocabularies

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:55.780
and loses appeal once batch sizes grow or heavy quantization is already in place.

